# Setup for tools/check_dequ_save_dc.sh (bd inc-2ok4): tools/keys/dequ-setup.keys
# with two changes. (1) The FIFTH attribute set, not the first: on seed 5 it
# gives the orc warrior DEX 13, a +1 modifier, a mid-Dex melee build. The first
# set gives DEX 17 (+3), which would pass a Reflex save about 70% of the time at
# any level and say nothing about a typical tank. (2) Cheat Death is switched on
# before Freeze Monsters, so a long run of failed saves cannot end the session.
# Everything else is dequ-setup.keys verbatim.
#
# Make the orc warrior every A_DEQU check uses, and freeze the monsters.
# Included by dequ-hardness-plain.keys, dequ-hardness-magic.keys,
# dequ-owner-immunity.keys, dequ-reach.keys, dequ-sunder.keys,
# favour-int32.keys, gear-item-exclusion.keys and item-flag-protection.keys.
# Old list: nonexistent file, three others missed; corrected 2026-09-12.
#
# The character is a male orc WARRIOR, CHAOTIC GOOD, worshipping whichever
# god the game offers, which on seed 5 is Khasrach. A warrior is deliberate:
# he starts with a weapon in hand, and every one of these checks is about
# what happens to a weapon. Chargen follows tools/keys/dequ-save-message.keys,
# known to reach the wizard menu on seed 5 with the pinned options file,
# tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat, used by these checks.
#
# This file said "neutral" until 2026-09-12. The description was the defect,
# not the character. He was deliberately left alone because seven checks have
# been measuring him for weeks.
#
# Race, subrace, class and alignment use @choose to select by name, so a
# class or race added to lib/ cannot change the character. See src/Wposix.cpp.
# Use a fixed seed: attribute sets have no names, and rolls decide the feats.
# Start-menu, attribute, yes/no, ENTER, Apply and wizard keys stay positional.
# Each standalone positional key has an @expect naming its screen; the feat,
# weapon, worship, domain, skill and wizard loops name their screens too.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so a summoned monster neither moves nor takes a turn of
# its own. It still ANSWERS a blow -- A_DEQU fires from inside the resolution of
# the player's own attack -- which is the whole point of these checks.

@expect "Initial Choices"
a       # Initial Choices: start menu is not a screen @choose reads.
@expect "Alter the character generation options?"
n       # No: this is a yes/no question.
@expect "Explore Mode. Continue?"
y       # Yes: this is a yes/no question.
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Warrior"
@expect "Which of the five attribute sets"
e       # Fifth offered set: DEX 13 (+1) on seed 5, a mid-Dex melee build
@choose "Chaotic Good"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Skill Manager"
ENTER   # Finish allocating ranks: a control key, not a named choice.
@expect "Confirm keep changes to skill ranks?"
y       # Keep the ranks: this is a yes/no question.
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Your personality archetype"
# Personality affects only the sheet banner, so its selection is not pinned.
ENTER   # Accept the selected personality archetype.
@expect "Entry Chamber"
y       # Dismiss the Entry Chamber description.
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Things in View"
ENTER   # Try to enter something here; the game refuses.
@expect "You can't go in anything here."
y       # Open the dungeon verb menu.
@expect "What do you want to do?"
a       # In-game [a] Apply: keep this key before ESC closes the menu.
@until "Things in View" ESC

# 'w' opens wizard mode and 'y' confirms it the first time. The pair is driven
# by @until rather than written out, because a keystroke swallowed by a prompt
# that was still up would spend every key after it on the wrong thing.
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w y
@expect "Wizard Mode Switches"
w       # Open Wizard Mode Switches.
# The switch list draws no cursor a screen dump can see, so this counts rows:
# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh, and the cursor opens on the first.
@expect "Freeze Monsters"
SPACE   # Cheat Death: NO -> YES, so retaliation cannot end the run
DOWN*10
@expect "all monsters are denied their"
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
@expect "Wizard Mode Options"
ESC     # Close the switches list: a control key, not a named choice.
